      {
        "id": "synth_step_1",
        "type": "synthesis",
        "name": "Hydrothermal synthesis and annealing",
        "procedure": "A cleaned NF (1.95×3 cm²) was first immersed in 30 mL DI water containing 5 mmol thiourea, 0.2 mmol sodium molybdate and 200 mg P123 in a 50 mL Teflon-lined autoclave and kept at 200°C for 12 h. After naturally cooling down to room temperature, the black product was taken out, rinsed with DI water and ethanol in sequence for six times and dried in vacuum at 60°C for 24 h. Finally, the obtained product was heated to 350°C at a heating rate of 10°C min⁻¹ and kept in a gas mixture of H₂ (40 sccm) and Ar (200 sccm) for 1 h.",
